<title>BRAZIL: Brazil CPMF &quot;check tax&quot; rules published.</title>
<headline>Brazil CPMF &quot;check tax&quot; rules published.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian government Monday published in its Official Journal the regulatory framework for a new financial transaction tax.</p>
<p>The so-called CPMF &quot;check tax&quot;, designed to raise some 400 million reais a month for the health services, comes into effect on January 23.</p>
<p>Foreign investors in Brazilian shares will have to pay the 0.2 percent levy at the start and end of their investments but not on stock transactions in between.</p>
<p>((-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-2230358))</p>
